 "constraints": [],
 "stem": "Calculate the standard deviation of the values: ${=vs[0]}, {=vs[1]}, {=vs[2]}, {=vs[3]}, {=vs[4]}$. Round your answer to 2 decimal places.",
 "answer": "fixed(sqrt(ss / 5), 2)",
 "solution": [
  "The mean is $\\bar{x}=\\dfrac{\\sum x}{n}=\\dfrac{{=vs[0]}+{=vs[1]}+{=vs[2]}+{=vs[3]}+{=vs[4]}}{5}=\\dfrac{{=s}}{5}={=m}$",
  "Squared deviations: $({=vs[0]}-{=m})^2={=(vs[0]-m)**2}$, $({=vs[1]}-{=m})^2={=(vs[1]-m)**2}$, $({=vs[2]}-{=m})^2={=(vs[2]-m)**2}$, $({=vs[3]}-{=m})^2={=(vs[3]-m)**2}$, $({=vs[4]}-{=m})^2={=(vs[4]-m)**2}$",
  "$\\sum (x-\\bar{x})^2={=ss}$",
  "$\\sigma=\\sqrt{\\dfrac{\\sum (x-\\bar{x})^2}{n}}=\\sqrt{\\dfrac{{=ss}}{5}}\\simeq {=fixed(sqrt(ss / 5), 2)}$"
 ],
 "proposed_misconceptions": [],
 "notes": "Mirrors the book example: five distinct values with whole-number mean, answer rounded to 2 d.p."
